{
	title: 'Structured private user profile and intro preferences',
	spec: `USER.md in the Hal home is a short, human-readable Markdown briefing about the user, not a rigid configuration schema. It starts with # User and uses predictable optional fields: Name, Language preference and Timezone. Optional sections Working preferences and Other durable context hold concise facts the user writes. Language preference distinguishes a default language or spelling variety from alternatives; a conversation in another language does not silently change the default. Timezone is a valid IANA identifier, not a fixed UTC offset. Unknown fields are omitted or explicitly Not specified, never invented or stored as angle-bracket placeholders. Existing freeform USER.md files remain valid and are included in prompts as before; no destructive migration or mandatory parser is introduced.

hal/intro (task vc) writes the answers of each run. It replaces the Name, Language preference and Timezone lines in place and adds the missing ones after the last such line (else after the # User header, else at the end), keeping every other line byte for byte, so the user's own notes survive a rerun. A skipped answer leaves the existing field unchanged. The file is created with the # User header when missing and written with mode 0600. A host timezone is never stored as the user's without the checks task vc describes; no location services, and no inference from account names, IP addresses or credentials.

Store only durable personal facts and preferences, never secrets, temporary progress or project-specific requirements. Actual profile contents never enter tracked tasks, examples, logs added for this feature or commits. USER.md stays gitignored and on the project rebuild keep list. The profile is optional and its absence does not prevent normal operation.

Focused checks cover rewriting fields in place while preserving other text, skipped fields, and the gitignore and rebuild protection. Avoid tests that merely restate template text.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Intro uses optional Markdown field lines, not a profile schema: it preserves freeform text byte-for-byte and appends only supplied values. Blank, Not specified, unknown, N/A and angle-bracket placeholders do not count as known fields. Legacy About sections remain valid; new optional context uses Working preferences. SYSTEM.md describes the same private briefing format and explicit-correction rule.',
		'Name, language and timezone skips use the durable named answer records, so host recovery does not re-ask them. The user never types an IANA name: the zone comes from the client (task wq) or a city lookup in Intl.supportedValuesOf, and profile.save writes atomically (temp file + rename through a symlink target) at most once per intro run. Later duplicate field lines of a rewritten label are dropped so the file has one value per field.'
	],
	needs: ['n2', 'vc'],
	foldInto: ['n2', 'vc']
}
